# SE-Blackboard

Multi-agent software engineering system with **Blackboard communication architecture** for automated code repair.

## Overview

This project investigates how different communication architectures affect multi-agent systems for automated code repair. It compares three communication modes across two pipeline topologies, evaluated on the [SWE-bench Lite](https://github.com/princeton-nlp/SWE-bench) benchmark.

### Communication Modes

| Mode | Description |
|------|-------------|
| **Message Passing** | Agents communicate via natural-language messages (traditional approach) |
| **Blackboard** | Agents read/write structured state from a shared blackboard |
| **Hybrid** | Combination of message passing and blackboard |

### Pipeline Topologies

| Topology | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| **Sequential** | Planner → Coder → Reviewer → Tester (with iterative feedback) |
| **Peer Debate** | Two Coders generate competing patches; Reviewer selects the best |

### Agents

- **Planner** — Analyzes the issue, identifies root cause, relevant files, and fix strategy
- **Coder** — Generates a unified-diff patch based on the analysis
- **Reviewer** — Reviews the patch and provides approve / needs_revision / reject verdict
- **Tester** — Applies the patch and runs tests via SWE-bench Docker harness

## Installation

### Prerequisites

- Python 3.10+
- Docker (required for SWE-bench evaluation)
- An [Anthropic API key](https://console.anthropic.com/)

### Setup

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone <repo-url>
cd se-blackboard

# Create a virtual environment
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate  # Linux/macOS
# or
.venv\Scripts\activate     # Windows

# Install dependencies
pip install -e ".[dev]"

# Configure your API key
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env and add your ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
```

## Usage

### Run tests

```bash
pytest
```

### Run an experiment

```bash
# Single configuration
python experiments/run_experiment.py --topology sequential --communication blackboard --issues data/selected_issues.json

# Single issue (for debugging)
python experiments/run_experiment.py --topology sequential --communication message_passing --issue-id django__django-11099

# All 6 configurations
python experiments/run_experiment.py --all
```

### Analyze results

```bash
python experiments/analyze_results.py
```

## Project Structure

```
se-blackboard/
├── config/
│   ├── settings.py             # Global configuration
│   └── prompts/                # Agent prompt templates
├── src/
│   ├── blackboard/             # Shared state schema & manager
│   ├── agents/                 # Agent implementations
│   ├── communication/          # Communication mode implementations
│   ├── topologies/             # Pipeline topology implementations
│   ├── evaluation/             # Metrics, IFS, SWE-bench runner
│   └── utils/                  # LLM client, structured logger
├── experiments/                # Experiment scripts
├── data/                       # Issue data & results
└── tests/                      # Unit tests
```

## Configuration

Key settings in `config/settings.py`:

| Setting | Default | Description |
|---------|---------|-------------|
| `MODEL` | `claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929` | Anthropic model to use |
| `TEMPERATURE` | `0` | Sampling temperature |
| `MAX_ITERATIONS` | `3` | Max fix-review-test loops |
| `MAX_TOKENS_PER_CALL` | `4096` | Max tokens per LLM call |
| `NUM_ISSUES` | `50` | Number of issues to evaluate |
